==Welsh==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|cy|myned}} {{qualifier|literary}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|North Wales}} {{IPA|[mɨ̞nd]|lang=cy}}
* {{a|South Wales}} {{IPA|[mɪnd]|lang=cy}}

===Etymology===
Suppletive verb; infinitive from {{etyl|wlm|cy}} {{term|mynet|lang=wlm}}, from {{etyl|cel-bry-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-bry-pro|*monetu}} (compare Cornish {{term|mones|lang=kw}}, Breton {{term|mont|lang=br}}), verbal noun of {{etyl|cel-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-pro|*mon-ī-}} (compare Middle Irish {{term|muinithir|lang=mga}} ‘goes around’), from {{etyl|ine-pro|cy}} {{m|ine-pro|*menH-}} (compare Umbrian {{term|menes|lang=xum}} ‘will come’, Lithunaian {{term|mìnti|lang=lt}} ‘to trample, scutch’). Indicative forms from {{etyl|cel-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-pro|*ag-o-}} ‘to drive’ (compare Old Irish {{term|agid|lang=sga}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|cy}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}} (compare Latin {{term|ago|agere|lang=la}}). Subjunctive forms from {{etyl|cel-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-pro|*el(l)-o-}} ‘to go’, from {{etyl|ine-pro|cy}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁el-}} (compare Ancient Greek {{term|ἐλάω|tr=eláō|lang=grc}} ‘to drive’, Old English {{term|ile|lang=ang}} ‘footsole’). 

===Verb===
{{head|cy|verb|irregular}}

# to [[go]]
#: {{usex|Mae hi'n '''mynd''' i Gaerdydd heno. |t=She's going to Cardiff tonight.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|'''Aeth''' hi ddoe.|t=She went yesterday.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|'''Awn''' ni ac yn edrych.|t=We will go and look.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|'''Aet''' ti i'r ysgol ar droed.|t=You went/used to go to school on foot.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|Mae'n angenrheidiol yr '''elwyf''' nawr.|t=It is necessary that I go now.|lang=cy}}

